        "description": "Protocol PDF p50, while Operation Enabled: 0x6040=0x0002 triggers quick stop; with 0x605A=0, decelerate by 0x6085 then enter Switch On Disabled. Other option values and timing are not defined in the reviewed PDF."
      },
      {
        "id": "FAULT-REACTION",
        "status": "unresolved",
        "description": "0x605E INT16 RW listed p15, but no supported values or physical response/timing. XML raw default is 2000 (LE integer 32); do not assume value 2."
      },
      {
        "id": "BRAKE-CONTROL",
        "status": "unresolved",
        "description": "No brake control/status object found in 79-object latest ESI or 56-page protocol. Manual PDF pp27-28 describes DC-supplied static holding brake, not EtherCAT release/apply sequence or timings."
      },
      {
        "id": "STO",
        "status": "not_evidenced",
        "description": "No safety-rated STO, SS1, SBC or FSoE evidence in examined protocol/ESIs/manual brake section. PDO disable and quick stop are ordinary controls, not STO."
      },
      {
        "id": "FAULT-RESET",
        "status": "documented",
        "description": "Protocol pp12 and55-56: 0x6040 bit7 rising edge / 0x0080 triggers system reset; runtime parameters revert to defaults and must be configured again."
      },
      {
        "id": "IGH-SAMPLE",
        "status": "not_integration_qualified",
        "description": "Official 260620 IGH source main.cpp uses legacy 0x5FFE padding, whereas latest ESI uses Rx0x2FFD/Tx0x2FFE; quick_stop/fault_reset flags are set by helper functions but not consumed by main loop. No source was executed."
      },
      {
        "id": "CAN-BRAKE",
        "status": "documented_separate_interface",
        "description": "CAN V4.4 provides 0x77 release and 0x78 lock plus 0x9A DATA3 command-state feedback. This is not a proven EtherCAT object mapping or mechanical brake position feedback."
      }
